  "title": "Exact integer and floating bit serialization, with explicit failure conditions",
  "tool_version_id": "aeneas-be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a",
  "trusted_assumptions": "F32/F64 are explicit 32/64-bit logical patterns; two executable std to_bits models preserve those patterns as unsigned words, with checked Lean value-preservation lemmas. Guards require original writer bodies and allow no other float operation. Kani checks std bit identity for every pattern and actual released writers with 6/10-byte buffers. Connecting these Rust checks to the Lean representation is reviewed, not mechanized; Rust nightlies differ. Official translation/standard integer and slice models, Lean, and Kani/CBMC are trusted. Mapped audits permit only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
